target/
www/pkg/
# The root .gitignore's `.gm/*` rule is anchored to the repo root (a gitignore
# pattern containing a slash is relative to the file that declares it), so it
# does NOT cover a nested .gm/ elsewhere in the tree. One landed here by
# accident (a `cd` into www/ persisted across Bash calls and a spool-boot
# command run from there registered this directory as its own gm project) and
# got committed. Scoped rule so it can't recur silently in this crate.
.gm/
